Z||000000||Patrick's Dad||12-24-2000||07:47 PM||||I know that a couple of you work for UPS in Norwood, so I had to vent....<P>Friday, I sent off a 2# package to Nashua NH via UPS Next Day, with Saturday Delivery. It was over $25.00 (our expense) to get it up there (from Norwood), so her husband would have it for Christmas. She called me today (Sunday), saying that it was not delivered. I tracked the package.... It's in Kentucky! It was scanned there at 10:45AM yesterday, and again at 8:15 today! I was upset, and she (understandably) was even more upset.<P>Who can I call on Tuesday to get this to her ASAP? Why did it go to KY! It apparently flew there from Windsor Locks, instead of Manchester, or something! I am not a happy camper, and may now rely on another shipping company when it needs to be there overnight and on a Saturday....||||reg||8
Z||000001||Seanh||12-24-2000||08:00 PM||||I hate Fedex and USPS, but I have not had any trouble with UPS yet. Fedex seems to get the package there on time, just not in one peice. USPS once left a pair of $1200 stereo speakers out side my door and they were rained on and damaged. It said right on the top of the box that is was to be signed for and was insured for $1500, but they just left it there. In the end they were "very sorry" and paid the insurance claim, and I have never seen that diliverery person again.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I would call up your local office and talk to them. If its not deliverered by the guarenteed date(if they give you one on next day)they should give you your money back. If not, dont let it die, they will eventually refund the price rather then deal with you continuosly. Trust me, I know from experience.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/transsig.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.<BR><I>"It's always in the last place you look." Of course it is. Why would you keep looking after you've found it? Do people do this? Who and where are they?</I>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Philphine||12-24-2000||08:22 PM||||louisville, ky. is THE ups hub. i've heard every thing ups ships comes through here and then goes where ever it's going.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cheever2||12-24-2000||08:49 PM||||I worked for Airborne Express for over 4 years.  They're real good, but they can treat packages pretty rough, <B>especially</B> anything marked "Fragile" or "Handle with care".  Almost everything goes into their private airport at Wilmington Ohio, where it gets sorted and put onto a plane to its destination, and gets there by morning.  Airborne wants volume customers (businesses), not door-to-door residential, although they wouldn't refuse it.  <BR>-<BR>But they are good.<BR>||||reg||6
